7: Independent Submission                                  H. Van de Sompel
8: Request for Comments: 7089                Los Alamos National Laboratory
9: Category: Informational                                        M. Nelson
10: ISSN: 2070-1721                                  Old Dominion University
11:                                                             R. Sanderson
12:                                           Los Alamos National Laboratory
13:                                                            December 2013
16:    HTTP Framework for Time-Based Access to Resource States -- Memento
18: Abstract
20:    The HTTP-based Memento framework bridges the present and past Web.
21:    It facilitates obtaining representations of prior states of a given
22:    resource by introducing datetime negotiation and TimeMaps.  Datetime
23:    negotiation is a variation on content negotiation that leverages the
24:    given resource's URI and a user agent's preferred datetime.  TimeMaps
25:    are lists that enumerate URIs of resources that encapsulate prior
26:    states of the given resource.  The framework also facilitates
27:    recognizing a resource that encapsulates a frozen prior state of
28:    another resource.
30: Status of This Memo
32:    This document is not an Internet Standards Track specification; it is
33:    published for informational purposes.
35:    This is a contribution to the RFC Series, independently of any other
36:    RFC stream.  The RFC Editor has chosen to publish this document at
37:    its discretion and makes no statement about its value for
38:    implementation or deployment.  Documents approved for publication by
